# Environment & Deployment Rules

## Environment Files — Never Committed

```
api/.env              → never committed (in .gitignore)
api/.env.example      → committed — all keys present, values empty or fake

dashboard/.env.local  → never committed
dashboard/.env.example → committed

extension/.env        → never committed
extension/.env.example → committed
```

## api/.env Variables

```bash
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3001

# Database
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/surfbud
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# Auth
JWT_SECRET=             # min 32 chars, generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET=   # separate secret for refresh tokens

# AI
GROQ_API_KEY=           # starts with gsk_

# CORS origins
DASHBOARD_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
EXTENSION_ORIGIN=chrome-extension://YOUR_EXTENSION_ID

# Optional
LOG_LEVEL=debug
```

## dashboard/.env.local Variables

```bash
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:3001
```

## Deployment Targets

```
api/        → Railway or Render (Node.js server)
             Build: npm run build
             Start: npm start
             Root directory: api/

dashboard/  → Vercel or Netlify (static SPA)
             Build: npm run build
             Output: dist/
             Root directory: dashboard/

extension/  → Chrome Web Store
             Build: npm run build:ext
             Output: dist/ (zip for submission)
             Root directory: extension/
```

## Path-Filtered CI — GitHub Actions

Each deployment is triggered ONLY by changes to its folder:

```yaml
# .github/workflows/deploy-api.yml
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
    paths:
      - 'api/**'
      - '.github/workflows/deploy-api.yml'

# .github/workflows/deploy-dashboard.yml
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
    paths:
      - 'dashboard/**'
      - '.github/workflows/deploy-dashboard.yml'
```

Changes to `dashboard/**` NEVER trigger the api pipeline. Changes to `api/**` NEVER trigger dashboard or extension pipelines.

## Production Checklist

Before any production deploy:
- [ ] All environment variables validated by Zod at startup (api)
- [ ] No `console.log` in committed code
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets anywhere
- [ ] `NODE_ENV=production` set in deployment environment
- [ ] CORS origins updated to production URLs (not localhost)
- [ ] JWT secrets rotated from development values
